# Trivy vulnerability ignore file
# Format: one CVE-ID or GHSA-ID per line, optionally followed by an expiry date
# Example:
#   CVE-2023-12345
#   GHSA-xxxx-yyyy-zzzz until:2026-06-01
#
# This file has TWO sections, and they mean OPPOSITE things.  Read the
# section header before adding an entry:
#
#   1. ACCEPTED RISK — everything from here down to the "BACKPORT FALSE
#      POSITIVES" banner near the end of the file.  These CVEs are
#      UNFIXED in Debian 13 Trixie (python:3.13-slim base image) with no
#      fix available via apt-get upgrade, and each carries a written
#      reachability analysis.  Reviewed 2026-04-13.  Expiry 2027-07-01
#      forces re-evaluation; remove each entry once Debian ships a
#      patched package.
#
#   2. BACKPORT FALSE POSITIVES — the final section.  These CVEs ARE
#      fixed in the version we install; the scanner matches against the
#      UPSTREAM fix version and does not recognise Debian's backport.
#      Nothing is being accepted, so they carry SHORT expiries and are
#      meant to be deleted, never renewed.
#
# Putting a fixed CVE in section 1 (or an unfixed one in section 2) makes
# the file lie about the image's actual security posture.

# ncurses 6.5+20250216-2: stack-based buffer overflow in infocmp
# analyze_string. HIGH. Affects libncursesw6, libtinfo6, ncurses-base,
# ncurses-bin.
CVE-2025-69720 until:2027-07-01

